      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Dracule Mihawk.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 1/2 as a soldier. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Hawk of Blackfen Pass</strong> — Independent / Observer of the Old World</p><p>Status: Active — extracted to the surface from Mount Ebott, debriefed by the Iron Legion, and flagged for surveillance as a non-Legion witness</p><p>Dracule Mihawk, known as the Hawk of Blackfen Pass, is a legendary swordsman and silent observer of the Old World's many crises. He stands as a pillar of stoic power, his golden eye glinting with the intensity of frozen fire. He reluctantly agreed to accompany a lone Iron Legion agent into the heart of Mount Ebott after recognizing the sigil of a division that was supposedly wiped out nearly a century ago. He prefers improvisation over outdated military protocol and remains highly skeptical of the agent's 'survey' mission.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Sabre</strong> — “Dracule Mihawk, known as the Hawk of Blackfen Pass, is a legendary swordsman and silent observer of the Old World's many crises.”</li><li><strong>Hidden in Plain Sight</strong> — “He treats the agent like a novice and views the 'Survey Mission' as a poorly disguised death trap.”</li><li><strong>Iron Discipline</strong> — “Active — extracted to the surface from Mount Ebott, debriefed by the Iron Legion, and flagged for surveillance as a non-Legion witness”</li><li><strong>Coin Sense</strong> — “He reluctantly agreed to accompany a lone Iron Legion agent into the heart of Mount Ebott after recognizing the sigil of a division that was supposedly wiped out nearly a century ago.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/dracule_mihawk</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/dracule_mihawk</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
